// Sandbox-only workspace. NOT used by consumers or by normal builds.
//
// Some build environments cannot reach the Go module proxy or the vanity
// hosts (go.opentelemetry.io, golang.org). This workspace redirects those
// modules to their GitHub mirrors. Activate it only in such an environment:
//
//   GOWORK=$(pwd)/go.work.sandbox GOPROXY=direct GOSUMDB=off make test
//
// `make SANDBOX=1 <target>` does the same. Keep go.mod free of these replaces.

go 1.24

use .

replace go.opentelemetry.io/otel => github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go v1.35.0
replace go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk => github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/sdk v1.35.0
replace go.opentelemetry.io/otel/trace => github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/trace v1.35.0
replace go.opentelemetry.io/otel/metric => github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/metric v1.35.0
replace go.opentelemetry.io/auto/sdk => github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-instrumentation/sdk v1.1.0
replace golang.org/x/sys => github.com/golang/sys v0.37.0
// gopkg.in is a blocked vanity host. A v3 tag cannot be a replace target on a
// non-/v3 GitHub path, so pin the commit of tag v3.0.1 as a pseudo-version.
replace gopkg.in/yaml.v3 => github.com/go-yaml/yaml v0.0.0-20220527083530-f6f7691b1fde
// yaml.v3's go.mod requires check.v1 (test-only); the graph still needs its go.mod.
replace gopkg.in/check.v1 => github.com/go-check/check v0.0.0-20161208181325-20d25e280405
